.policy "ruff-pt021-pytest-fixture-finalizer-callback" revision 2
.description "Prefer a yield with the cleanup after it over a finalizer callback in a pytest fixture; reserve the callback for fixtures that build resources on demand."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PT021 (flake8-pytest-style): a fixture taking `request` that registers cleanup with
// `request.addfinalizer(…)` instead of yielding and cleaning up after the yield. One finding per fixture, at the
// last such call Ruff's walk sees (pytest_seen: not in nested defs, not under expressions other than calls).
//   @pytest.fixture
//   def db(request):
//       conn = connect()
//       request.addfinalizer(conn.close)     ← PT021
//       return conn
#include "python/pytest.rr"
//   pytest_fixture(f, d, e), pytest_seen(f, n), exc_dotted(e, s); names: params(f, x, i)

.violation PT021(at: node) code "PT021"
    "Return the fixture value with `yield` and move this cleanup, and any other registered finalizer, after it. Keep the callback if cleanup must run even when later setup code raises."
    suppress ruff "PT021"
PT021(c) :- finalizer(f, c), !later_finalizer(f, c).
.decl later_finalizer(f: node, c: node)  // Ruff keeps the last call its walk sees
later_finalizer(f, c) :- finalizer(f, c), finalizer(f, c2), earlier(c, c2).
.decl finalizer(f: node, c: node)
finalizer(f, c) :- pytest_fixture(f, _, _), params(f, "request", _), pytest_seen(f, c), kind(c, "call"),
    field(c, "function", g), exc_dotted(g, "request.addfinalizer").
